    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d602">

                <pb facs="0573" n="563" xml:id="pg563"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0140/886</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hamilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-15">September 15, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I believe that there is no need
                    for us to interpose objection to the Commander in Chief’s proposal to reduce the
                    number of Marines at Shanghai from 857 to 800 and those in north China from 260
                    to 200.</p>
                <p>If you concur, I shall so inform Captain Schuirmann with the request that this
                    move be carried out in such a way as to minimize in so far as practicable
                        publicity.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d602-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">axwell</hi>] M. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">amilton</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d602-f1" n="71" xml:id="d602-f1-content">
                <p>Capt. Schuirmann was so informed on September 16. Notation by President Roosevelt
                    “O.K. F.D.R.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
